  "worked_solution": "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-3.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(1,-3,8)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(1,-3).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(1,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,-3) & =\\frac{{1}^{2}+1}{{1}^{2}(-3)^{2}}+(-3)\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}-3(1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{25}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
